==German==

===Etymology===
Literally, "when [[Easter]] and [[Pentecost]] fall on the same day". By definition, Pentecost always falls seven weeks after Easter.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|de|De-wenn Ostern und Pfingsten auf einen Tag fallen.ogg|Audio}}

===Adverb===
{{de-adv}}

# [[when pigs fly]] ([[never]], expressed idiomatically).

